architecture inverse-compiler
  canonical_name InverseCompiler
  family execution
  domain Execution / Institutional Synthesis
  layer execution/compiler
  semantic_question Given a TargetObligation, which owner-backed predicates and declared transformation alternatives could lawfully close its residual?
  purpose A non-owning compiler between TargetObligation, ClosureAlgebra and egglog. It reads arbitrary native TargetObligation PredicateRefs, saturates declared transformation algebra, Pareto-rejects dominated alternatives, applies an explicit preference policy, and lowers a selected candidate into typed cross-owner residuals without writing commitments, authority, evidence, reservations or effects itself.
  maturity implemented
  consumes TargetObligation
  consumes ClosureAlgebra
  consumes Authority
  consumes InformationPolicy
  publishes PredicateRef
  publishes ClosureProgramIR
  node_types PredicateRef
  node_types TransformationIR
  node_types ClosureProgramIR
  edge_types requires
  edge_types establishes
  edge_types retracts
  edge_types equivalent_to
  invariant a PredicateRef addresses an existing owner, subject, expected state and temporal/evidence/authority boundary; it is never a cached assertion that the expected state currently holds
  invariant a ClosureProgramIR is a candidate projection across owners, not a new plan-state store; WorkGraph, CommitmentGraph, ResourceActivation and EffectKernel retain their own transitions
  invariant non-monotone transformations retain requires, establishes, retracts, consumes, produces, commitments, rights, conflicts, obligations, economic deltas, reversibility and compensation cost through CUE, Zig, egglog extraction and native descriptors
  invariant egglog searches only equivalences declared after CUE validation; a found equivalence is not truth, authority, provider admission, reservation or permission to execute
  invariant owner evaluation reads the native owner state plane at compilation time and records a receipt of that answer; it never writes an actual_state shadow field
  invariant the only semantic-owner-to-native evaluation binding is the CUE OwnerAdapter table compiled by Zig into typed adapter/state opcodes; runtime C may execute an opcode but may not select an owner or expected state by comparing declaration strings
  invariant owner_query is declared with each CUE OwnerAdapter state and carried losslessly into generated native grammar; CommerceChain's fifteen distinct canonical stages and CommitmentGraph's five lifecycle states therefore remain owner query families rather than hand-picked branches
  invariant a temporal capacity predicate is answered only by ResourceReservation over the requested window, never by resource activation, provider presence or a quote
  invariant WorkGraph lowering emits proposed cross-owner residuals naming capability, authority recheck, ProtocolContract pattern, commitment pattern, resource pattern, effect kind and compensation posture; the separate admit boundary rereads effect-time authority and every declared prerequisite before exposing an admissible aperture, while neither boundary grants authority nor prepares an effect
  invariant projected WorkGraph mission/node identities derive from target and predicate identity, never target string length or another lossy presentation property
  invariant reconciliation reevaluates every declared owner PredicateRef and may request proof-owned target closure only when every predicate holds and the target explicitly declares a matching ProofFrontier source frontier
  invariant an `InverseCompiler:closure_program` FactDelta handoff is consumed only by the native inverse worker, which reruns owner-backed synthesis/reconciliation and atomically marks the envelope handled; it emits no effect attempt and carries no planning-time authority across the boundary
  forbidden_inference a well-formed predicate address -> the owner currently satisfies it
  forbidden_inference an egglog-equivalent closure -> an admissible, selected or executable plan
  forbidden_inference a preferred transformation -> current authority or a completed effect
  interacts target-obligation-compiles-predicate-residual
  interacts inverse-compiler-saturates-equivalences
  interacts inverse-compiler-reads-native-owner-state
  interacts inverse-compiler-lowers-selected-residual-work
  interacts inverse-compiler-reconciles-proof-frontier
  source_path schemas/control/inverse-compiler.cue
  source_path schemas/control/owner-predicate-contracts.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSemanticOptimizer/tools/compile_inverse_program.zig
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSemanticOptimizer/generated/inverse-programs.egg
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSemanticOptimizer/generated/inverse_programs.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSemanticOptimizer/src/main.c
  source_path deploy/systemd/bonfyre-inverse-compiler-worker.service
  source_path deploy/systemd/bonfyre-inverse-compiler-worker.timer
  witness cmd/BonfyreSemanticOptimizer/tests/inverse_compiler_test.sh proves fixture subjects/program registries are absent from generated production algebra, unknown semantic fields fail Zig compilation, non-monotone fields survive CUE-to-native lowering, CommerceChain's fifteen stages and CommitmentGraph's five lifecycle states are emitted with CUE-declared numeric queries, and the generated egglog algebra plus static e-class extraction are valid
  witness cmd/BonfyreSemanticOptimizer/tests/live_inverse_test.c creates arbitrary native target:storm-closure-742 PredicateRefs, proves an `InverseCompiler:closure_program` handoff drains into generic native residual synthesis and is retained as an atomic handled receipt, verifies FRONTIER_SATISFIED does not change the target from OPEN, proves an effect aperture is admitted only while its authority edge remains current then refused immediately after revocation, and completes a second arbitrary target through retained ForeignTwin receipt -> directional EvidenceGraph support -> ProofFrontier -> proof-owned TargetObligation closure
  known_gap recursive prerequisite expansion, compensation enactment, actual external adapters, complete post-effect observation scheduling and incremental affected-cut repair remain separate passes. The compiler emits their typed residual requirements but does not claim they occurred.

