architecture pure-execution-tier
  canonical_name PureExecutionTier
  family execution
  domain Execution
  maturity measured
  semantic_question Which backend should reduce this pure search space, and did the backends agree on what it contains?
  # Bonfyre decides what may be computed; a reducer computes the pure search
  # space; Bonfyre decides what the result means and whether anything may happen
  # because of it. A backend here is a compiler target beneath the organs, never
  # an owner beside them: it holds no truth, identity, authority or money, and it
  # cannot perform an effect. HVM2 having no external-call layer is not a
  # limitation for this purpose, it is the property that makes it safe.
  node_types ExecutionProfile
  node_types PureJob
  node_types DifferentialReceipt
  edge_types lowers_to
  edge_types compared_against
  state_types available
  state_types vendored_unbuilt
  state_types not_installed
  invariant purity is checked before dispatch and never inferred from a job's name; a reducer that could reach outward would be a second effect path beside the one the estate governs
  invariant the purity scan runs over field names and values with the declaration field removed, and matches whole words; scanning the whole document matched effect inside effect_class and refused every correctly declared pure job, which is a guard rejecting exactly the input it exists to admit
  invariant a backend absent from this machine is reported unavailable with its reason, never skipped; a skipped backend leaves the comparison and its absence reads as agreement
  invariant a backend that only exercised a job's shape reports no result; an interaction count printed beside a result computed elsewhere measures the runtime and answers nothing
  invariant agreement is undetermined rather than assumed when fewer than two backends produced a result
  invariant the differential harness is itself tested by corrupting a lowering and requiring the disagreement to surface; an agreement check that cannot fail is decoration
  invariant declared availability is a claim about the estate and presence on PATH is a fact about this process, and the two are recorded apart; a vendored but unbuilt runtime is never mistaken for a running one
  invariant a lowering states the shape of predicate it can express and refuses input outside it rather than approximating; the boolean encoding refuses a non-boolean field
  forbidden_inference agreement between backends -> correctness
  forbidden_inference an interaction count -> wall time or energy
  forbidden_inference a candidate frontier -> a decision
  forbidden_inference constant cost for a non-inspecting function -> constant cost for a function that branches on its argument
  forbidden_inference vendored source -> an available backend
  computational_form reduction
  native_format json
  source_path scripts/pure-job.mjs
  source_path scripts/pure-series.mjs
  witness scripts/tests/pure-native.test.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/execution_profile.json
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/pure_tier_test.sh
  measured hvm2 2.0.22 reduced the retained-and-observed frontier over 30 live twins to 26 survivors at 320 interactions, identical to the reference backend
  known_gap the lowering expresses boolean predicates only; arithmetic and ordering are not expressible in it, and the operator node form was probed and not established
  invariant a mutation test corrupts exactly one reducer, never the shared decode; breaking every backend equally leaves them agreeing and proves nothing
  invariant a backend that produced no result carries a reason whatever the reason is; an errored backend rendering as a blank cell is the same silent disappearance the unavailable case was written to prevent
  invariant a superposition is binary, so a candidate space is nested, and the index tree and the verdict tree are nested identically; a different shape pairs a candidate with another candidate's answer
  measured hvm4 4.0 built from vendored source reduced the same 30-twin frontier to the same 26 survivors at 188 interactions against hvm2's 320 on this encoding
  forbidden_inference fewer interactions on one encoding -> a faster or better runtime (the encodings differ, and interactions are not wall time)
  forbidden_inference hvm4 -> a more parallel hvm2 (its own banner calls it a sequential runtime, so it is a different calculus rather than a successor)
  invariant a backend answering with an aggregate is checked against the reference's own aggregate and kept out of the set-equality vote; the two are not being asked the same question, and counting them together lets a weaker agreement stand in for a stronger one
  invariant a backend states what it answered, so an aggregate is never read as a frontier
  measured bend-lang 0.2.38 compiles the candidate predicate and folds it over a tree, returning 26 survivors and index checksum 394 in agreement with the reference; its generated core is structurally the lowering that had been written by hand, which is what validates the hand version
  known_gap bend answers an aggregate rather than the frontier, because a fold yields one value; recovering the set through Bend would need a different program and has not been written
  known_gap hvm4 describes itself as pre-launch, so agreement on one job is evidence for promotion and not promotion; a single cohort is not a differential series
  invariant the tier asks ResourceAdmission before dispatching to any backend, and a backend admission will not place is refused with that reason recorded; the two were built beside each other and neither consulted the other, so a job declaring money work over institution-private data reached reducers on a machine cleared only for public input
  invariant a backend is not placed by default; when the admission decision cannot be obtained, nothing runs rather than everything
  measured a job declaring money work over institution-private data now reaches no reducer and still runs on the reference where the data lives, while public discovery work still reaches both reducers
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/execution_profile.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/compute_site.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/representation_profile.json
  known_gap the tier could not be run from a checkout. It reads execution_profile, compute_site and representation_profile rows from the CMS, and none of those three content types existed in the repository -- the schemas lived only on the deploy host. From a clone the tier refuses with "no execution_profile rows are readable", which reads as the backends being missing when what is missing is their declaration. All three are now in version control.
  known_gap an unrecognised max_data_scope rendered as "cleared for institution_private, this input is public" -- a wider clearance appearing to refuse narrower data, which sends a reader looking for a policy bug. The site had written institution_private where the vocabulary says institution-private, and a typo was being reported as a rule. Fail-closed was right; the message was wrong and now names the unrecognised term.
  known_gap the lowering is total on booleans. A predicate needing arithmetic or ordering is refused rather than approximated, which is correct and is also the wall between this tier and the financial class of work: money is comparison and summation, so nothing about thresholds, balances or allocations can be expressed here yet.
  known_gap HVM4 calls itself a sequential Interaction Calculus runtime, so what this tier gets from it is optimal sharing, confluence, and a reducer with no external-call layer -- not parallelism. Reading interaction-net work as "parallel by default" would be the wrong reason to reach for it.
  witness architecture/tests/numeric_lowering_test.sh
  internal_calculus numeric comparison in the net: HVM4 operators distribute over superpositions, so a whole candidate space compares against a threshold in one reduction and the predicate is computed by the backend rather than handed to it
  internal_calculus subset lattice by distinct superposition labels: n labels give all 2^n combinations as one term, each total paired with a mask identifying its subset
  invariant a numeric clause compares integers only. A price is carried as micro-USD, because a float disagreeing with the reference in the last bit presents as a backend disagreeing about money and costs more to chase than the scale costs to carry
  invariant a backend that cannot express a numeric clause refuses the job rather than dropping the clause; dropping it would leave the backend answering an easier question and calling the result agreement
  known_gap the boolean lowering evaluates the predicate in Python and hands the net the verdicts to fan out. The differential still catches a broken lowering -- corrupting one backend surfaces as disagreement -- but no backend computes what the predicate means, so a predicate that is wrong is wrong identically in all four places. The numeric lowering is the first where the comparison happens in the net.
  known_gap superposition enumerates the subset lattice; it does not prune it. Measured on real price-book data the cost per branch is roughly constant and mildly improving -- 22.5 interactions per subset at n=4, 17.6 at n=16 -- and the collapse emits one line per branch, so 2^n output. Reading this as a knapsack solver that beats brute force would be laundering: at n=16 the net returned 264 feasible subsets identical to brute force, and it did so by walking all 65,536.
  known_gap what the net buys here is expression, not complexity: the whole lattice is one declarative term over a fixed operator vocabulary, with no loop and no enumeration written by hand. That is a real property and it is not a speedup.
  witness architecture/tests/plane_rank_reduce_test.sh
  interacts plane-ranks-into-pure-reduction
  invariant the survivor set does not depend on the order candidates are presented in; a reducer whose answer moves with the sequence is letting the ranker decide the result
  known_gap Bend answers with a sum over candidate indices, which is positional, so its checksum moves when the order moves. That is correct for a positional aggregate and it is a trap: compared against a reference computed in a different order it reads as a backend disagreeing about a pure computation when nothing disagreed.
  witness architecture/tests/chain_portfolio_test.sh
  internal_calculus subset budget: a candidate space plus an integer field and a budget yields every subset whose total is within it, by enumeration in the reference and as one superposed term in the net
  invariant the subset lattice refuses past twenty candidates rather than returning part of it; the collapse emits one line per subset, so this is a wall and not a tuning knob, and a truncated lattice answers a different question while looking like the same one

architecture profile-runner-legibility
  canonical_name ProfileRunnerLegibility
  family execution
  domain Execution
  maturity measured
  semantic_question When a scheduled profile fails, does the failure say what failed and why, where the scheduler can see it?
  # Three hypercycle units sat in `failed`. The journal held
  # "Main process exited, code=exited, status=1/FAILURE" and nothing else,
  # because the runner wrote every diagnostic to per-tool log files whose
  # existence and location you had to already know.
  node_types ProfileRun
  node_types ToolReceipt
  edge_types explains
  state_types passed
  state_types failed
  invariant a failing run names each failing tool and that tool's own last error on stderr, so the scheduler's journal carries the reason rather than the exit code alone
  invariant a receipt is appended with one write under O_APPEND; concurrent profiles sharing one JSONL had already interleaved two lines into JSON valid from neither
  invariant the failure summary skips a receipt line it cannot parse and says how many it skipped, because a diagnostic that dies on its own input buries the failure it exists to report
  invariant an assertion message carries the values it compared; expected notification attempts and actioned state named the half that was fine while attempt_count was 156
  forbidden_inference a failing unit -> a defect in the code it runs
  forbidden_inference a green unit -> an institution that acted
  computational_form derivation
  native_format json
  source_path tools/estate/checkpoint93-profile-runner.sh
  source_path tools/estate/checkpoint93-profile-receipt.mjs
  witness tools/estate/checkpoint93-profile-receipt.test.mjs verifies the default runner invokes Bun helpers, concurrent O_APPEND writes retain whole receipt rows, malformed lines are counted and prior runs excluded, and the final error diagnostic remains visible without a scheduled profile execution
  source_path tools/estate/live-institutional-closure-flow.ts
  witness the three units were restarted after the repair; cloud-placement and provider-credit completed, and graph-closure printed its own reason into journalctl
  measured cloud-placement and provider-credit failed only because execCommand threw on a missing aws binary rather than returning the result its type declares; both pass with the binary still absent
  measured graph-closure still fails and should: the operator overview reports 157 notification attempts and 0 actioned, so notifications are sent and none has ever been actioned
  known_gap the estate holds 271 tools under /opt/bonfyre/tools with no version control and one counterpart in the checkout; four are mirrored under tools/estate and nothing keeps the rest in step
